{{project}}
============

API server generated by TurboGears2 quickstart-api command.

This project demonstrates best practices for implementing JSON-based APIs with TurboGears2.

Features
--------

- **RESTful API**: Clean REST controller implementation with ``tg.RestController``
- **Dual Authentication**: Support for both cookie-based and Bearer token authentication
- **Automatic OpenAPI**: API documentation automatically generated via ``tgext.apispec``
- **Validation**: Automatic parameter validation with ``@validate`` decorator
- **JSON Responses**: Native JSON support with proper content-type headers

Quick Start
----------

1. Install the project in development mode::

    pip install -e '.[development]'

2. Run the test suite::

    python -m pytest

3. Initialize the database and create demo users::

    gearbox setup-app

4. Run the development server::

    gearbox serve --reload --debug

5. Open your browser to http://localhost:8080; it redirects to the API demo page.

Configuration Profiles and Checks
---------------------------------

Quickstart creates ``development.ini`` for local development and ``test.ini``
for tests; ``test.ini`` references the development configuration. Quickstart
does not generate ``production.ini`` because production configuration is
deployment-specific.

For a compact project check::

    $ gearbox tginfo summary --project . --config development.ini
    $ gearbox tginfo routes --project . --config development.ini
    $ python -m pytest --collect-only -q

{{if sqlalchemy and migrations}}
Database Migrations
-------------------

Alembic is included in the development dependencies. Migrations are usually
not needed during ordinary development. To read the current database revision
without changing it, run::

    $ gearbox migrate -c development.ini db_version

Creating a revision, autogenerating a revision, and upgrading a database are
deliberate schema or deployment operations::

    $ gearbox migrate -c development.ini create 'Describe the schema change'
    $ gearbox migrate -c development.ini autogenerate 'Describe the schema change'
    $ gearbox migrate -c development.ini upgrade
{{endif}}

Quickstart also installs optional coding-agent skills into the project-local
``.agents/skills/`` directory. To install them for Claude Code instead, run
``gearbox tgskills --claude`` from the project root; this installs only
``.claude/skills/``. Delete the installed skills directory if you do not use
that assistant.

API Endpoints
-------------

- ``GET /api/movies`` - List all movies
- ``POST /api/movies`` - Create a new movie
- ``GET /api/movies/{id}`` - Get a specific movie
- ``PUT /api/movies/{id}`` - Update a movie
- ``DELETE /api/movies/{id}`` - Delete a movie
- ``GET /demo`` - API demo landing page
- ``GET /demo/admin`` - Admin-only endpoint (requires 'manage' permission)
- ``GET /api/openapi.json`` - OpenAPI specification
- ``GET /api/docs`` - Interactive API documentation (Redoc)

Authentication
--------------

This API supports two authentication methods:

1. **Bearer Token**: Use the ``Authorization: Bearer <token>`` header
2. **Cookie Auth**: Use the standard TurboGears login flow

Demo users created by ``gearbox setup-app``:

- **manager**: password=managepass, token=abc123def456ghi789jkl012mno345 (has 'manage' permission)
- **editor**: password=editpass, token=pqr678stu901vwx234yz567abc890

Example using Bearer token::

    curl -H "Authorization: Bearer abc123def456ghi789jkl012mno345" http://localhost:8080/api/movies

Example using cookie auth::

    # Login first
    curl -v --cookie-jar cookies.txt -d "login=manager&password=managepass" http://localhost:8080/login_handler
    
    # Then access API with cookie
    curl --cookie cookies.txt http://localhost:8080/demo/admin

Cleanup
-------

Once you're ready to build your own API, you can remove the demo parts::

    rm -rf {{package}}/controllers/api/movies.py {{package}}/controllers/demo.py \
           {{package}}/model/movie.py {{package}}/websetup/bootstrap_movies.py \
           {{package}}/templates/demo \
           {{package}}/tests/functional/test_movies.py \
           {{package}}/tests/functional/test_auth.py
    gearbox patch {{package}}/controllers/root.py DemoController -d
    gearbox patch {{package}}/controllers/api/__init__.py Movie -d
    gearbox patch {{package}}/controllers/api/__init__.py movies -d
    gearbox patch {{package}}/model/__init__.py Movie -d
    gearbox patch {{package}}/websetup/bootstrap.py bootstrap_movies -d

Run the commands from the project root (the directory containing
``development.ini``).

The demo tests (``test_movies.py`` and ``test_auth.py``) are removed
together with the demo parts because they exercise the endpoints above.

